%% alt: Flowchart of the canonical transformation order. The raw file is loaded and typed, then copied so the raw table is never written to. Five stages follow in order: structure (duplicates, reposts, the unit of a row), values (text, booleans, dates, impossible numbers), missing (count, name the mechanism, drop or impute or flag), outliers (a rule and a threshold, flag before dropping), and encode and scale (categories to numbers, numbers to one range). Every stage returns a frame and a log row, and the fitted parameters of the missing, outlier and encoding stages are stored so the same pipeline can be applied to next month's file without being fitted again.
flowchart TD
  R["Raw file<br/>never written to"] --> L["Load and type<br/>schema, validate"]
  L --> C["copy()<br/>work on a copy"]
  C --> S1["1 Structure<br/>duplicates, reposts<br/>what is one row?"]
  S1 --> S2["2 Values<br/>text, booleans, dates<br/>impossible numbers"]
  S2 --> S3["3 Missing<br/>count, name the mechanism<br/>drop, impute or flag"]
  S3 --> S4["4 Outliers<br/>choose a rule<br/>flag before dropping"]
  S4 --> S5["5 Encode and scale<br/>categories to numbers<br/>numbers to one range"]
  S5 --> M["Model-ready table<br/>+ decision log"]
  S3 -.-> P[["fitted parameters<br/>medians, lists, min and max"]]
  S4 -.-> P
  S5 -.-> P
  P -.-> N["Next month's file<br/>apply, never refit"]
